     Okay.  I had an above-average start going; I'd successfully gotten my
pet to rob most of a small store even without a leash or tripe ration (this
isn't the spoiler, but: if you want a particular item, wait until your dog
picks it up and then leave the shop; the dog is more likely to bring it to
you.  A slight convenience; I still had to try three or four times before
I finally got ahold of that blessed purple potion the shopkeeper wanted
400gp for.  Ironically, it was a potion of paralysis).  Anyway, by that time
the level had several monsters on it, one of which happened to be a wererat.
During the combat, I "felt feverish" so, being a Priest, I remembered (here's
the spoiler) than my clove of garlic fixed that.
     Here's where things went wrong both this time and, apparently the
previous time: last time, I happened to be a rat (or was it a jackal) and
though I "felt purified" I didn't change form until either I prayed or
got down to 0hp; can't remember which.  This time I, being at about half
hp, was still human, and I got a "You return to human form!"
     Now, I know that funny things are supposed to happen when you polymorph
into a human, as apparently I was doing, but methinks the game was being
excessively pissy when ALL of my attributes went down to 3!
     Needless to say, my game is worthless.  There's no way in hell (for
that matter, on dlvl 2 where I am, either) that I'm going to be able to
survive until I can pray with a strength of 3; there were already two
mosters beating on me when I saved the game (I wasn't able to do anything
with a hex editor; it wasn't readily apparent where the abilities were,
even if the file isn't encrypted, which is most likely is) and both of
them appeared to be doing substantial damage (I decided to quaff a potion
after this happened just to see what it was, and it was of hallucination,
so I don't know what they were).
     Ah well, at least it wasn't one of those dlvl-25 crashes on a level
62,345 character with -83.62 AC....

